[00:23.76]O God, you know my rest and waking,
[00:30.04]When I lie down and when I rise anew.
[00:38.52]You search my thoughts, my inmost inclination,
[00:45.76]The words I speak, the ways I walk,
[00:50.16]you know them too.
[00:54.22]You saw when I was made in secret,
[01:01.48]My very bones not hidden from your sight.
[01:09.12]You saw my form; its parts were down in writing.
[01:16.84]I love the wonder of your ways
[01:20.58]and praise your might.
[01:24.62]Your knowledge, God, is wondrous, awe-inspiring;
[01:31.46]Of this my soul is very well-aware.
[01:39.66]If I should fear that darkness might enfold me,
[01:47.16]Your spirit, God, would find me, even there.
[01:55.26]Where could I hide from you, Jehovah,
[02:02.34]Or be concealed, be hidden from your face?
[02:09.80]Not in the Grave nor in the highest heaven,
[02:17.34]Not in the dark nor in the sea;
[03:31.56]there is no place.
